# ============================================================================
# setup/link.conf.local.example
#
# Copy this to setup/link.conf.local (gitignored, never committed) to
# override values from link.conf for THIS HOST ONLY. Use it for things that
# legitimately differ between air and gs -- WIFI_TXPOWER (ground station
# usually has a bigger battery and a heatsink) and QGC_HOST are the normal
# candidates.
#
# ⚠ Do NOT put RADIO-section values here (WIFI_CHANNEL, BANDWIDTH, MCS_INDEX,
#   STBC, LDPC, SHORT_GI, LINK_DOMAIN, WIFI_REGION). Those must match on both
#   ends, and install.sh warns if link.conf.local overrides one of them.
#   install.sh also prints a SHA-256 of the effective radio section so you
#   can compare both ends at a glance without transmitting the config itself.
# ============================================================================

# Example: ground station has an external 12V->5V supply and a heatsink,
# so it can run higher power than the air unit's bench USB feed.
# POWER_SOURCE=external
# WIFI_TXPOWER=1500

# Example: QGroundControl runs on a separate laptop on the LAN instead of
# on the ground-station Pi itself.
# QGC_HOST=192.168.1.50
